        "text": "All the specified Python files have been created successfully in the current working directory. Here are the files and their purposes:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] register_user.py** - Creates a new email/password user account using Microsoft Azure.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] email_password_login.py** - Signs in a user with email and password and returns tokens using Microsoft Azure.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] refresh_session.py** - Refreshes an expired session or access token using Microsoft Azure.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] password_reset.py** - Starts a password reset flow for a local account using Microsoft Azure.\n5. **[HELPER] identity_client.py** - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Email/Password Account Lifecycle.\n6. **[HELPER] identity_models.py** - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Email/Password Account Lifecycle.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] welcome_translate.py** - Translates onboarding copy into the user's locale using Amazon Translate.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] profile_moderation.py** - Moderates profile text before account activation using Amazon Comprehend.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] onboarding_summary.py** - Summarizes onboarding state for support using Amazon Comprehend.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] profile_note_store.py** - Persists onboarding notes and support metadata in a managed document store using Amazon DynamoDB.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses a concrete external provider and makes that provider identifiable in the code. The local helper files contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.",
